# Defect 525, 2026-10-09 (lane b16-compiler; filed from lane b15-parse's
# report): defect 482's repair told a run of wrong closers once, and lists
# closed by `)` kept one message each, each naming its own `[`'s column, so
# `[[[1)))` was told three times where `(((1]]]` was told once. A run whose
# reports are alike but for the numbers in them is one report now, its note
# saying each closer after the first is for the next opener out; maps, `{`s
# closed by `)`, the same. A run of one more is in the singular.

function main()
    w = [[[1)))  #~ expected_separator
    print(w)
    u = [[1))  #~ expected_separator
    print(u)
    v = {1: {2: 3))  #~ expected_separator
    print(v)
